{"name":"Smokestack","hex":"#beb2a5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"smokestack","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A conduit or group of conduits atop a structure allowing smoke to flow out, as on a steam locomotive, ship, factory, or power plant using fossil fuels."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smokestack"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chimney","blocks":[{"text":"A chimney is an architectural ventilation structure made of masonry, clay or metal that isolates hot toxic exhaust gases or smoke produced by a boiler, stove, furnace, incinerator, or fireplace from human living areas. Chimneys are typically vertical, or as near as possible to vertical, to ensure that the gases flow smoothly, drawing air into the combustion in what is known as the stack, or chimney effect. The space inside a chimney is called the flue. Chimneys are adjacent to large industrial refineries, fossil fuel combustion facilities or part of buildings, steam locomotives and ships."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chimney"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Kamer_boven_poort_-_Geverik_-_20077791_-_RCE.jpg/250px-Kamer_boven_poort_-_Geverik_-_20077791_-_RCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Kamer_boven_poort_-_Geverik_-_20077791_-_RCE.jpg/500px-Kamer_boven_poort_-_Geverik_-_20077791_-_RCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Kamer_boven_poort_-_Geverik_-_20077791_-_RCE.jpg/250px-Kamer_boven_poort_-_Geverik_-_20077791_-_RCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKamer_boven_poort_-_Geverik_-_20077791_-_RCE.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Chimney.stack.london.arp.jpg/250